<h1>ISFDB Derived Information</h1>

<ol>
  <li> <a href="http://HTMLBASE/agestuff.html">Age Graphs</a>. A page
  of graphs showing age-related information such as: age at publication
  of first novel, age at publication of any novel (or shortfiction and
  essays), age at publication of award-nominated publication, and age
  at publication of an award-winning publication.
  <p>
  <li> <a href="http://HTMLBASE/top100.html">Top 100 Lists</a>.
  These are top 100 lists based on awards data; novels, shortfiction,
  publication, and author lists are available.
  <p>
  <li> <a href="http://HTMLBASE/oldest.html">Oldest Living List</a>.
  A list of the oldest living authors, editors, and artists in the
  database.
  <p>
  <li> <a href="http://HTMLBASE/oldest_nl.html">Oldest Non-Living List</a>.
  A list of the oldest no-longer-living authors, editors, and artists in the
  database.
  <p>
  <li> <a href="http://HTMLBASE/youngest.html">Youngest Living List</a>.
  A list of the youngest living authors, editors, and artists in the
  database.
  <p>
  <li> <a href="http://HTMLBASE/youngest_nl.html">Youngest Non-Living List</a>.
  A list of the youngest no-longer-living authors, editors, and artists in the
  database.
  <p>
  <li> <a href="http://HTMLBASE/mostsf.html">Most-Reviewed Books</a>.
  Lists of genre-related books that were most reviewed by genre-related
  publications.
</ol>

